Model Response:
```json
{"thought":"I found that budget.json links to events via link_to_event. October Meeting has event_id 'recggMW2eyCYceNcy'. I need to find all budgets for this event, then find all expenses linked to those budgets that are approved.","action":"execute_python","action_input":{"code":"import json\nimport csv\n\n# Read budget.json\nwith open('json/budget.json', 'r') as f:\n    budget_data = json.load(f)\n\n# Find budgets for October Meeting (event_id: recggMW2eyCYceNcy)\noctober_meeting_budgets = [b for b in budget_data['records'] if b.get('link_to_event') == 'recggMW2eyCYceNcy']\nprint(\"Budgets for October Meeting:\")\nfor b in october_meeting_budgets:\n    print(f\"  {b['budget_id']}: {b['category']} - spent: {b['spent']}\")\n\n# Get budget IDs\nbudget_ids = [b['budget_id'] for b in october_meeting_budgets]\nprint(f\"\\nBudget IDs: {budget_ids}\")\n\n# Read expense.csv and filter for approved expenses linked to these budgets\nexpenses = []\nwith open('csv/expense.csv', 'r') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        if row['link_to_budget'] in budget_ids and row['approved'] == 'true':\n            expenses.append({\n                'description': row['expense_description'],\n                'cost': float(row['cost']),\n                'budget_id': row['link_to_budget']\n            })\n\nprint(f\"\\nApproved expenses for October Meeting: {len(expenses)}\")\nfor e in expenses:\n    print(f\"  {e['description']}: ${e['cost']}\")\n\n# Group by type and sum\ntype_totals = {}\nfor e in expenses:\n    desc = e['description']\n    if desc not in type_totals:\n        type_totals[desc] = 0\n    type_totals[desc] += e['cost']\n\nprint(\"\\nTotal by expense type:\")\nfor t, total in type_totals.items():\n    print(f\"  {t}: ${total:.2f}\")\n\n# Create result table\nresult_rows = [[t, round(total, 2)] for t, total in type_totals.items()]\nprint(f\"\\nResult rows: {result_rows}\")"}}
```
